  "name": "rrns-arith-lib",
  "notes": "A VHDL library for using the Redundant Residue Number System (RRNS). RNS (without the initial R) is an alternative number system that uses residues (remainders) of divisions by different moduli (divisors) to represent numbers. By adding more moduli without increasing the dynamic range of possible numbers, errors can be detected.\r\nIt is licensed under CERN-OHL-P-2.0.\r\n\r\nThis is an archived version of the library, for current developments check https://github.com/IMS-AS-LUH/rrns-arith-lib",
